  "goodToKnow": "Der Rundfunk is broadcasting, radio and television together. Germany's öffentlich-rechtlicher Rundfunk (public broadcasting) includes ARD, ZDF and Deutschlandradio, and regional broadcasters like the Bayerischer Rundfunk and WDR. Every household pays the Rundfunkbeitrag, about 18 euros a month, whether or not it owns a TV. Literally, Rundfunk means sparks sent all around, from early radio transmitters."
